<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">El Mozote massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The El Mozote massacre was the killing of more than 800 civilians, many of them children, by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlacatl-battalion">Atlacatl Battalion</a> of the Salvadoran army in and around the village of El Mozote, in Morazán <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, on 11–12 December 1981. It was the largest massacre of the Salvadoran civil war. Long denied by the Salvadoran and American governments, it was confirmed by exhumations and the UN Truth Commission.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/el-mozote-massacre.jpg" alt="El Mozote massacre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Efrojas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emmemorial800.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Elite units such as the Atlacatl Battalion committed massacres, notably at <b>El Mozote</b> in December 1981, and in November 1989 soldiers murdered six Jesuit priests at the Central American University in San Salvador.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-el-salvador">Republic of El Salvador · Military</a></li></ul></section>
